esting thing about  all this is that we don't actually know  exactly what causes muscle fatigue what  causes muscles to fail what we do know  is that more muscle equals more glycogen  in other words if you have bigger  muscles you can store more glycogen and  you can go for longer bodybuilders who  train specifically for hypertrophy who  aim for muscle size will automatically  be capable of larger rep ranges because  they have more muscle and a bigger  resource to draw from  [Music]  large rep ranges work because they give  us metabolic stress as well as muscle  damage and these are two great signals  that trigger muscle growth with that  said of course the glycogen lactic acid  system also creates more metabolic waste  products that contribute to muscle  fatigue we used to think that lactate  was responsible for this sensation of  burn that would interfere with our  ability to contract our muscles however  we now know that lactate is not the  enemy lactate in fact gets shuttled away  from the muscles and then converted back  into pyruvate and back into glucose and  ions are thought to contribute to  acidity that might interfere with  contractions however this isn't 100  either in fact some studies looking at  acidity levels in the muscles find that  they generally remain within acceptable  limits even when we're fatigued so it's  unlikely that that's fully responsible  for muscle fatigue either and the really  interesting thing is that we don't know  100 what actually causes muscle fatigue  there are many other factors that may  play a role such as ionic changes to the  excitation contraction coupling and many  more chances are it's a combination of  these things however what we do know is  that a better circulatory system is  going to help you to get rid of waste  products and provide your muscles with  the nutrients they need and this leads  me nicely onto the other aspect of  strength endurance which is just  endurance you know cardio aerobic  fitness and you're